<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρβω</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf., exc. plpf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεφόρβειν</span> (v. infr.):—Poet.
		Verb (used by <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
		</span></i> (v. infr.) and v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Criti.</u>
			115a
		</span></i>, and later Prose, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφερβε φονέα ἑαυτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Syr.</u>
					62
				</span></i>
			); <i>feed, nourish,</i> of the earth, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				30.2
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθεμα] ὕδωρ φέρβει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					2.73
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ᾽ ἔφερβε σὸς δόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					869
				</span></i>
			; of shepherds, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. βοτά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					75
				</span></i>
			; c. gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ βοτάνης ἐπεφόρβει βοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					105
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>preserve,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρώϊον οἶκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					377
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be fed, feed upon</i> a thing, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέξω δαῖθ᾽ ὑφ᾽ ὧν ἐφερβόμην</span>
			shall make food for those by whom <i>I fed myself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				957
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδε φέρβεται ἐκ σέθεν ὄλβου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					30.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>eat, consume,</i> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ψυχὴ τὸ σῶμα φέρβεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					6.5.2
				</span></i>
			; metaph., <i>feed on,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					827
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to be fed, live,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1016
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>enjoy, have,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέσσονα ἁλικίας νόον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					5.110
				</span></i>
			:—late in 
				Act.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρβειν πρηΰτατον . . νόημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.643
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
